-- #1111 A-2.12 (#1319 unit 2) — THE "FEATURE PRESENT, UNRELATED CODE STILL
-- BEHAVES" CELL for the RECORD tables, which is the fixture shape `AGENTS.md`
-- requires of any change that adds a PROGRAM-GLOBAL TABLE.  Unit 2 adds three:
-- `universeRecordIdentsRef`, `universeRecordCollidedRef` and
-- `universeFieldCollidedRef`.  A fixture that exercises the feature proves nothing
-- about that hazard — "your feature works perfectly and something unrelated breaks"
-- is the failure it produces — so the assertion here is about a module that takes no
-- part in the collision.
--
-- The graph: `rcolla` and `rcollb` each declare a NAMED-FIELD variant spelled `Dup`,
-- at different types and with different field types, with NO import relationship
-- between them.  `usea` means rcolla's (reached only through `RA(..)`, which never
-- spells `Dup`), `useb` means rcollb's (named by name), and `bystand` means its OWN
-- — while importing rcolla's constructors with `(..)` and using one of them, so its
-- answer is not green by construction.  See `bystand.mdk` for exactly which rung of
-- the scope ladder it discriminates.
--
-- Expected output, derived BY HAND before any capture and independently of any
-- engine:
--   ra  = unRA (Dup { dx = 7 })                      = 7
--   rb  = unRB (Dup { dx = "b" })                    = "b"
--   bys = unPlain (Dup { px = 5 }) + unRA (ACount 2) = 5 + (2 * 10) = 25
-- so `7`, `b`, `25`.
import usea.{ra}
import useb.{rb}
import bystand.{bys}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  let _ = putStrLn (intToString ra)
  let _ = putStrLn rb
  putStrLn (intToString bys)
